[0m[0m
[38;5;10mprint_foo[0m in the Rust took [38;5;10m*const foo_t[0m and immediately did [38;5;10m&*foo[0m, forming a reference. [38;5;10malignof(foo_t) == 4[0m, so a misaligned pointer aborts the process under Rust's alignment check. gcc compiles the same field access to a plain [38;5;10mmov 0x4(%rax),%esi[0m, which loads the unaligned value and prints it normally. An external caller passing a misaligned struct got output from the C and [38;5;10mSIGABRT[0m from the Rust.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
